Hi Drea, here is the updated running order for the interview day. Please share the timings with the people who are coming so we can keep the room quiet while each interview is recorded.

We will arrive at eight to bring in the lighting and test the sound. The first interview can start at nine. Each slot includes a few minutes to settle in, check the microphone and explain where to look. There is a break after the second interview, then we will record the remaining two before lunch.

For the room, could you arrange:
- four ordinary chairs, without wheels if possible;
- a small table for water;
- a place to leave coats away from the camera;
- the display samples you want in the background.

We will film the demonstration after lunch, once the interview equipment is packed away. Please tell us if the sample needs time to warm up. We can use that interval to record the room details and any close shots of the controls.

Thanks,
Ellor
